<title>JAPAN: Japan's GDP rises 1.0 pct in October/December.</title>
<headline>Japan's GDP rises 1.0 pct in October/December.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's gross domestic product (GDP) rose a real 1.0 percent in the October/December quarter from the previous quarter, or an annualised 3.9 percent, the Economic Planning Agency (EPA) said on Thursday.</p>
<p>Quarter on quarter figures</p>
<p>		    October/December		   PREV QTR</p>
<p> Real GDP	+1.0, annualised +3.9	+0.3, annualised +1.3</p>
<p> Real GNP	+0.6, annualised +2.5	+0.7, annualised +2.9</p>
<p> Nominal GDP   +0.5			   +0.4</p>
<p> Nominal GNP   +0.1			   +0.8</p>
<p> (Year on year)		October/December     PREV QTR</p>
<p> GDP deflator		     -0.1 pct	 +0.1 pct</p>
<p>(Real data in percentage of contribution to overall GDP)</p>
<p> Domestic demand		   +0.6	     +0.1</p>
<p>   Private			   +1.2	     +0.2</p>
<p>   Public			    -0.7	     -0.1</p>
<p> External demand		   +0.4	     +0.2</p>
<p>   Exports goods/services	+0.5	     +0.2</p>
<p>   Imports goods/services	-0.1	     +0.0</p>
<p>Breakdown of domestic demand contribution:</p>
<p>Private</p>
<p>   Personal outlays		+0.7	     -0.1</p>
<p>   Housing			   +0.2	     -0.0</p>
<p>   Capital spending		+0.3	     +0.3</p>
<p>   Inventory changes	     -0.0	     -0.0</p>
<p>Public</p>
<p>   Government outlays	    +0.1	     +0.1</p>
<p>   Capital spending		-0.7	     -0.2</p>
<p>   Inventory changes	     -0.0	     -0.0</p>
<p>(Real data - changes in expenditures, quarter on quarter)</p>
<p>Private</p>
<p>   Personal outlays		+1.2	     -0.2</p>
<p>   Housing			   +4.0	     -0.5</p>
<p>   Capital spending		+2.1	     +2.0</p>
<p>   Inventory changes	    -25.9	     -8.5</p>
<p>Public</p>
<p>   Government outlays	    +0.6	     +1.3</p>
<p>   Capital spending		-7.5	     -2.0</p>
<p>   Inventory changes	    -42.3	    -68.2</p>
<p> External			  +147.5	   +507.8</p>
<p> Exports			     +4.3	     +1.6</p>
<p> Imports			     +1.1	     -0.3</p>
<p>(Note: Due to rounding, figures may not tally. Also, figures smaller than two decimal places are not shown.)</p>
</text>
